    "EstimatedProjectEndLife": "2026",
    "Audience": "Companies in the public safety sector.",
    "text": "Nancy Mace unveils immigration-focused public safety plan during a campaign stop at the state house Tuesday, lowcountry congresswoman and gubernatorial candidate Nancy Mace laid out her public safety agenda for SC. Published: Jan. 6, 2026 at 6:21 pm EST|Updated: 6 hours ago Email this link Share on x (formerly Twitter) Share on Pinterest Share on LinkedIn Columbia, S.C. (WIS) -U.S. Rep. Nancy Mace on Tuesday outlined part of her public safety platform as part of her campaign for South Carolina governor, saying immigration is the top concern among voters. Mace proposed legislation that would penalize sheriffs and jail administrators who refuse to cooperate with federal immigration authorities. While members of Congress cannot introduce state bills, Mace said the proposal reflects what she would pursue if elected governor. “There should be a mechanism with teeth that allows the governor to remove a sanctuary sheriff because I want to make sure when im governor that it never happens again in the state of South Carolina,” Mace said during a news conference at the statehouse. Mace acknowledged the bill does not yet have a sponsor in the South Carolina legislature, noting she drafted it over the holidays. Feel more informed, prepared, and connected with WIS. For more free content like this, subscribe to our email newsletter , and download our apps . Have feedback that can help us improve? Click here . Copyright 2026 WIS. All rights reserved. Most read"
}

